{"title":"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two puppies, Walter and Stanley, are growing at different but constant rates. Walter’s mass is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> kg and he is growing at a rate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> kg/month. Stanley’s mass is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> kg and he is growing at a rate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/c/40cba44ffc429fc98e11a1605ced22243b655f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> kg/month. What will Stanley’s mass be when it is equal to Walter’s?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/6/576769145650c1084361c4e91a1b23b5a019933c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 24 \\text { kg} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 28 \\text { kg} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 32 \\text { kg} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 36 \\text { kg} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 42 \\text { kg}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"510\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can create functions. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/9703e10f151c26e976f124951c28a2dac5f1884d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> represent Stanley's mass after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> months and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/b/1fbf2dc9f4233f5839c7f4334e8eedda044ea649.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" /> represent Walter's mass after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> months.\n</p><p>Since Stanley is originally <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> kg and is growing at a rate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/c/40cba44ffc429fc98e11a1605ced22243b655f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> kg per month, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5af9ad70f4a39ff60eaefee45e9f7aa2a5867a1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(x) = 2.5x + 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/2/712b829623695b0d43e35ecc0fae22ac79839d73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w(x) = 2x + 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>We can now see at what <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> value these intersect at by setting the equations equal to each other:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/b/0eb1db57ef69c9ece5437be78477586e53dd5c60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(x) = w(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/d/53dde2838eb02945e5102519d0c758894e91703a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2.5x + 6 = 2x + 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"151\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94ba3b18ff676c5c074f6f0a63bbe81e3bc7a672.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.5x = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/6/de6d8cacad133519e78ba6bca876f2e0053c319e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 6 \\times 2 = 12 \\text{ months}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"178\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>We can now plug-in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/7/c975e64a5ed6e7d28e6f651e8102d070a417d4c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> into one of the equations (either one would work) to see what weight Stanley would have, as both would be equal:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e3d61e3ec47926e2e358a6ab362db0161047e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(12) = 2.5 \\times 12 + 6 = 30 + 6 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 36 \\text{ kg}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"348\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/8/9c8310f1ab05223567860c6e83276938f128adab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w(12) = 2 \\times 12 + 12 = 24 + 12 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 36 \\text{ kg}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"357\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CEMC G